# What `vercel deploy` must not upload.
#
# Git-based deploys clone the repo and are already covered by .gitignore, but a
# CLI deploy uploads the working directory as it is — which here meant 629 MB of
# embeddings and a 1.2 GB Python virtualenv, and failed outright on Vercel's
# 100 MB per-file limit.
#
# Only apps/web, packages/shared and scripts are npm workspaces; nothing below
# is needed to build the site.

# Model artefacts. taxa_embeddings_v1.npy alone is over the per-file limit, and
# it belongs to Modal, not to the web build.
data/

# The ML service. Python, and its virtualenv, neither of which Vercel runs.
apps/ml/

# Local database state.
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/

# Build output and local noise — Vercel builds its own.
.next/
**/.next/
*.log
apps/web/e2e/shots/

# The Vercel CLI's own link directory, which can contain pulled env files.
.vercel/

# Environment files. A CLI deploy uploads the working directory, and the
# Vercel CLI leaves out only .env.local and .env.*.local by itself: the local
# .env holds the model service's token and the cron secret, and
# apps/web/.env links to it. The same list as .gitignore
# (apps/web/test/secrets.test.mjs holds the two together).
.env*
**/.env*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
